Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Of course, I can help you with that.  An “if/then” statement is used to make a decision based on a condition. In C, you use the “if” statement to test for a condition, and then make a decision based on whether that condition is true or false. Here is the basic pattern:

if (condition) {
   // execute this if the condition is true
} else {
   // execute this if the condition is false
}

In this example, if the condition is true, the code inside the first set of curly braces will be executed. Otherwise, if the condition is false, the code inside the other set of curly braces will be executed.
